{"shortDescription":"Spot basis bids for soybeans were steady to mixed in the US Midwest on Monday as weekend rains slowed harvest progress in the northern half of the crop belt, spot checks showed.Basis values are quoted against CBOT futures in cts/bu:NOTE: 0 = Option price, UNC = Unchanged, UNQ = UnquotedNC = Not com…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Spot basis bids for soybeans were steady to mixed in the US Midwest on Monday as weekend rains slowed harvest progress in the northern half of the crop belt, spot checks showed."]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The spot basis for soybeans at a crushing facility in Lincoln, Nebraska, jumped by 35 cents to 85 cents a bushel over Chicago Board of Trade November (SX26) soybean futures, reflecting strong demand for soybeans delivered into the region's processing plants this week."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Bids were significantly lower for soybean delivery to Lincoln next week and through October."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["In contrast, the soybean basis fell by 30 cents a bushel at a crusher in Decatur, Indiana. While still in the early stages, the Indiana soybean harvest was 3% complete as of September 13, ahead of the five-year average of 2%, according to the US Department of Agriculture."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Ahead of the USDA's weekly crop progress report due later on Monday, analysts polled by Reuters expected the agency to show the US soybean harvest as 12% complete and the corn harvest as 13% complete."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Corn basis bids were mostly steady. Among the exceptions on Monday, the basis improved by 5 cents a bushel at an ethanol plant in Linden, Indiana, while the basis fell by 3 cents at Davenport, Iowa, on the Mississippi River."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["CBOT November soybea